==German==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|goh|de}} {{term|jār|lang=goh}}, from {{etyl|gem-pro|de}} {{m|gem-pro|*jērą}}, from {{etyl|gem-pro|de}} {{m|ine-pro|*yōr-}} < {{m|ine-pro|*yeh₁r-}}. Compare Dutch {{term|jaar|lang=nl}}, English {{term|year|lang=en}}, Danish {{term|år|lang=da}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/jaːɐ̯/|lang=de}} {{a|standard}}
* {{IPA|/jaː/|lang=de}} {{a|widespread}}
* {{audio|De-Jahr.ogg|Audio|lang=de}}
* {{rhymes|aːɐ̯|lang=de}}
* {{homophones|ja|lang=de}} {{a|not according to standard pronunciation}}

===Noun===
{{de-noun|n|Jahres|Jahre|pl2=Jahr|Jährchen Dative Plural - Jahren}}

# [[year]]

====Usage notes====
The unchanged plural ''Jahr'' is chiefly colloquial (or poetic). It is almost exclusively used after numerals, mainly in adverbial constructions such as ''zwei Jahr später'' – "two years later" (instead of proper standard: ''zwei Jahre später'').

